# Neptunium · Np · gate 93

**Neptunium** (Np) is element **93** of the periodic table — a **actinide**, period 7, group f-block, f-block, solid at standard conditions, atomic weight **[237] (most stable isotope)**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
The first element beyond uranium; a trace in every spent fuel rod.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **93** falls on **0:1 — first valley** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **0**. That state is *the first reach of emptiness toward one — potential, charge, the rising edge* — the nature of emergence here is **electrical**. Neptunium is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — electrical
This emergent carries the **electrical** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#3fd0e0`.

